/P 277 0 R
/E (ZAMCOPS is a member of CISAC, the international organisation that regulates CMOs worldwide, whose rules allow members to check with other societies on remittances for music played in their countries. Elsewhere, governments had implemented regulations compelling radio and TV stations to play 90% local and 10% foreign music, hence remittances came only some time after collection. ZAMCOPS had been pushing for this regulation in Zambia, and it was being tabled as a bill in Parliament.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [20]
>>
