<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 281 0 R
/E (When COVID started, the board faced a very difficult decision: lay off employees or put them on half salaries to maintain operations. Laying staff off would have meant sanctions from the Ministry of Labour, whose minister had stated that nobody was to lose employment due to COVID. For three years the organisation accrued staff salary arrears, unpaid until last year when its financial position improved; ZAMCOPS has started paying them off, as an employment compliance issue. During that period ZAMCOPS closed its Kitwe office, laid off two employees and transferred one to the Lusaka office.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
